{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetLv8UzBScWeBwY8BUad","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All 21 tests passed. The command ran successfully with no failures or errors.\n\n**Command:** `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/`\n\n**Result:** \n- Tests run: 21\n- Failures: 0\n- Errors: 0\n- Skipped: 0\n- Build: SUCCESS\n\n**Tests executed:**\n- OrderControllerTest: 11 tests (7 new tests added for cancel functionality)\n- ShipmentControllerTest: 6 tests (1 new test added for cancelled order rejection)\n- CustomerControllerTest: 3 tests (unchanged)\n- SampleServiceApplicationTests: 1 test (unchanged)\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — Build succeeded with all tests passing.\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 4 original OrderControllerTest tests plus 3 CustomerControllerTest and 5 ShipmentControllerTest tests continue to pass.\n3. ✅ **`POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's `CREATED` shipments** — Implemented in OrderController.kt with test \"cancels all CREATED shipments when cancelling an active order\" verifying the behavior.\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Uses the same `ConflictException` and `ResourceNotFoundException` pattern, GlobalExceptionHandler converts to standard error envelope with code and message.\n5. ✅ **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a `CONFIRMED` shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused** — Tests added:\n   - \"cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds and changes nothing\" ✅\n   - \"returns 409 when trying to cancel an order with a CONFIRMED shipment\" ✅\n   - \"order stays ACTIVE when cancel fails due to confirmed shipment\" ✅\n   - \"returns 404 when cancelling a non-existent order\" ✅\n   - \"returns 409 when creating a shipment for a cancelled order\" ✅\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — No changes to pom.xml.\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified files related to order and shipment features plus the shared `api` package as allowed.\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — ✅ Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field to Order with default value. This is necessary and backward-compatible.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — ✅ \n   - Added dependency injection of ShipmentRepository (necessary to find and update shipments)\n   - Added cancel endpoint with proper logic:\n     - Returns 404 if order not found\n     - Returns 200 if already cancelled (idempotent)\n     - Checks for CONFIRMED shipments, throws 409 if any exist (atomic: fails before any write)\n     - Cancels all CREATED shipments\n     - Cancels the order\n     - Returns 200 with the cancelled order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — ✅ Added `findByOrderId()` method to retrieve shipments for a given order. Necessary for the cancel operation and for the check when creating shipments.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — ✅ \n   - Added dependency injection of OrderRepository (necessary to check order status)\n   - Added check before creating shipment: if order exists and is CANCELLED, throw 409\n   - Maintains existing behavior when order doesn't exist (proceeds with shipment creation)\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — ✅ Added two new error codes:\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` — for rejecting shipment creation on cancelled order\n   - `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` — for rejecting order cancellation when confirmed shipment exists\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — ✅ Added comprehensive tests:\n   - \"creates an order with ACTIVE status\" — verifies default status\n   - \"cancels an active order and returns it with CANCELLED status\"\n   - \"cancels all CREATED shipments when cancelling an active order\"\n   - \"cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds and changes nothing\" (idempotency)\n   - \"returns 409 when trying to cancel an order with a CONFIRMED shipment\"\n   - \"order stays ACTIVE when cancel fails due to confirmed shipment\"\n   - \"returns 404 when cancelling a non-existent order\"\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — ✅ Added test:\n   - \"returns 409 when creating a shipment for a cancelled order\"\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are satisfied and all tests pass.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint for customers to cancel active orders until a carrier confirms a shipment, with proper status tracking, idempotency, atomicity, and error handling.\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt: Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field with default value to track order lifecycle\n- OrderController.kt: Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with business logic for cancellation, confirmation check, and shipment cancellation\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId() method to retrieve shipments for a given order\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added check to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT error codes\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 7 tests covering cancel behavior, idempotency, atomicity, and error cases\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 1 test verifying rejection of shipment creation for cancelled order\n\nTests:\n- \"creates an order with ACTIVE status\" — verifies new orders start in ACTIVE state\n- \"cancels an active order and returns it with CANCELLED status\" — verifies basic cancel operation\n- \"cancels all CREATED shipments when cancelling an active order\" — verifies cascading shipment cancellation\n- \"cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds and changes nothing\" — verifies idempotency (retry safety)\n- \"returns 409 when trying to cancel an order with a CONFIRMED shipment\" — verifies atomicity check\n- \"order stays ACTIVE when cancel fails due to confirmed shipment\" — verifies nothing changes on failure\n- \"returns 404 when cancelling a non-existent order\" — verifies error for unknown order\n- \"returns 409 when creating a shipment for a cancelled order\" — verifies post-cancellation shipment rejection\n\nVerification: Ran `./mvnw test` from sample-service/ — 21 tests executed, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS\n\nNot done: Nothing — all acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests passing, no unrelated files modified."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3360,"cache_read_input_tokens":37304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3360},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f8c01f9-32ca-48ee-9404-e2af86c81a87","uuid":"b275f98d-78d0-414a-9bad-0dce5ebaa52e","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:32:45.984Z","request_id":"req_011CetLv7n53x7c16fqXagT9"}
